            <ArticleTitle>Childhood wheeze while taking propranolol for treatment of infantile hemangiomas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>713-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ppul.21603</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While it is recognized that beta-blockers can exacerbate asthma symptoms in older children and adults, there are few descriptions of a similar effect in infants. We describe three infants who developed wheeze during treatment with a beta-blocker for infantile hemangiomas and conclude that physicians should inquire about respiratory symptoms in this group of children.</AbstractText>
